Moves the `types` condition to the top of `exports`.

The bundler of our declaration files matches conditions in order, like
Node.js does: it stops at `import` and looks for `lib/esm/index.d.ts`,
which doesn't exist. TypeScript tries the next conditions in this case,
which is why only the build breaks. Without the patch, the build either
fails or keeps `import ... from 'lossless-json'` in our declaration files,
which breaks types for users, as the package is bundled.

diff --git a/package.json b/package.json
index b4d8bac6dcf9dc875c694dd29a0bb34c1baeeeca..29d85b39408571a2c7bf390884dc4b11589fa5b6 100644
--- a/package.json
+++ b/package.json
@@ -9,9 +9,9 @@
   "sideEffects": false,
   "exports": {
     ".": {
+      "types": "./lib/types/index.d.ts",
       "import": "./lib/esm/index.js",
-      "require": "./lib/umd/lossless-json.js",
-      "types": "./lib/types/index.d.ts"
+      "require": "./lib/umd/lossless-json.js"
     }
   },
   "repository": {
